## 🛠️ Swagger OpenAPI Specifications (Backend Endpoints)

The Spring Boot backend exposes several API endpoints documented at /swagger-ui.html. Below is the detailed resource structure:

- **POST /api/auth/login**: Authenticates users and returns a JWT bearer token.
- **GET /api/patterns**: Returns a list of all distributed system design patterns (Public).
- **GET /api/patterns/{id}**: Fetches detailed information for a single design pattern (Public).
- **POST /api/patterns**: Inserts a new design pattern (Admin only).
- **PUT /api/patterns/{id}**: Modifies properties of an existing pattern by ID (Admin only).
- **DELETE /api/patterns/{id}**: Removes a design pattern from the repository (Admin only).
- **GET /api/stats**: Retrieves aggregate counts of patterns, categories, and logs (Public).

